  "notes": [
    "SOURCE: TI SNVSBD5D Fig 9-1, Tables 9-2/3; SNVU621D Fig 4-1 (Q1 EVM).",
    "FUNCTION: VIN_PROTECTED -> 5.1 V nominal / 5 A. No 6 A peak rating.",
    "MODIFICATION: 6.8 uH; 100k/24.4k FB; 50 V raw-rail caps; BIAS grounded; input PGOOD gates EN.",
    "RATIONALE: input margin, ripple/tolerance headroom and buck-fault exposure. VCC is internal use only.",
    "CRITICAL LOOP: C203 VIN1-PGND1 and C204 VIN2-PGND2 immediately at U201; join both PGND to AGND.",
    "Feedback stays before disconnect. Keep SW away from FB and Kelvin routes. No physical layout exists.",
    "OPEN: exact RJR footprint, guaranteed effective L/C, load transient and thermal validation. See BUCK_DESIGN.md."
  ],
  "source_document": "docs/evidence/r2/BUCK_DESIGN.md",
  "schematic_notes": [
    "DATASHEET: L201 = Wurth 74437636351002, 10uH; 2 plated slots per drawing001.000 (2025-02-07).",
    "CALCULATED: 100k / 24.4k local feedback = 5.098361 V nominal. No remote sense or setpoint increase.",
    "JP201 separates native BUCK_SW from L201_IN. Remove while unpowered for independent fixture isolation / injection.",
    "C205 bootstrap return stays on native BUCK_SW. TP201 / TP202 paired return pads are sense only.",
    "ASSUMED qualification box: total local input C 10–30uF; Ldiff 5–12uH through 100A. These are not manufacturer guarantees.",
    "OPEN: nonlinear magnetic behavior, biased capacitance, startup/inrush, loop stability, ripple and thermal limits.",
    "TEST HOOK — design proven on bench; evidence NOT RUN. Dummy load only; isolated coupons before integrated faults."
  ],
